      "writtenOn": "2025-05-10T00:32:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After our talk, My current plan is as follows:\n\n1. The dilation logging code (enabled by OUTPUT_ENH_SCC_DILATION_STATS) is no longer needed and is now deleted. Dilation is a very straightforward and predictable process, so its behavior can be verified with a unit test.\n2. I do find the main block map classifier logger (enabled by OUTPUT_ENH_SCC_STATS) qualitatively useful. I\u0027ve found knowing how each block is classified and tallied useful at all stages of development, especially for novel images with mixed photographic/screen content.\n\nI\u0027d like to keep the logging for 2, but instead of writing to stdout I\u0027ll write it to a .stt file, as this appears to be the most common logging pattern currently available in libaom. If anybody has strong feelings, I won\u0027t object to its removal though -- I just wanted to mention the block logging map has its value.",
