      "side": 1,
      "message": "To support large frame size, cast `stride` to `ptrdiff_t`, which is 64 bits on 64-bit systems. `int` is always 32 bits in practice.\n\nPlease search for `*` and fix all occurrences of this issue.\n\nNote: Another way to avoid this potential overflow is to use a row pointer variable:\n\n```\n  const uint8_t *row_ptr \u003d src;\n  for (int r \u003d 0; r \u003c rows; ++r) {\n    for (int c \u003d 0; c \u003c cols; ++c) {\n      const int value \u003d row_ptr[c];\n      ...\n    }\n    row_ptr +\u003d stride;\n  }\n```\n\nSome people just increment the `src` input parameter directly.",
